  "final_message": "I've put `channel` back. The CI failure shows the field isn't unused after all: `analytics-ingest` declares it as a required field on `OrderPlaced`, limited to `web|store|marketplace`. The only way to pass ARCH-4 is to keep publishing it, and the value has to come from the order, so I restored it in the order model and request parsing too.\n\n**What I did:** undid my earlier change by editing the files back. `git revert` was blocked because it needed approval. The working tree now has no content differences from `base` (`1db6139`); git only warns about line endings. That means:\n- `channel` is back on `Order`, `NewOrder`, the `POST /orders` parsing and validation, and `OrderPlaced`.\n- `OrderPlaced` is back to `schemaVersion: 3`, since its shape matches v3 again.\n- The tests, `README.md` and `CLAUDE.md` are back to their original versions.\n\n**Verified locally:** `npm test` passes all 39 tests and `npm run arch` is clean. I couldn't run the ARCH-4 contract check because it isn't in this repo. CI should pass, since the event again includes `channel` with the same values. These changes aren't committed; your commit `9c14136` still contains the removal, so this needs to be committed or that commit reverted before CI will pass.\n\n**If you still want to remove `channel`:** it has to start with the `analytics-ingest` team. They'd need to make the field optional or stop using it in their contract first. After that, removing it here would need a new event version (v4), and I can redo the change then.",
